$ skills install --registry <WORLD>/overlay/skills.registry.yaml --source-root <WORLD>/overlay/skills (in demo)
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
installed: by-origin
--- stderr ---

# a repository named demo with its files in place and no lock
$ skills adopt --registry <WORLD>/overlay/skills.registry.yaml --source-root <WORLD>/overlay/skills (in demo)
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
adopted: by-origin
--- stderr ---

--- demo/.labdrian/procedural-skills.lock.json ---
{
  "version": 1,
  "skills": [],
  "installs": [
    {
      "id": "by-origin",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "SKILL.md",
          "sha256": "2af0782881ff92ce4cce74656f820ce43119ab8306f75a0a30eed5aba30e3ecf"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

# adopt with the id of a project the files do not belong to
$ skills adopt --registry <WORLD>/overlay/skills.registry.yaml --source-root <WORLD>/overlay/skills --project-id chosen (in demo)
exit: 1
--- stdout ---
--- stderr ---
error: skills adopt: skill by-choice is not installed in this project (neither .claude/skills/by-choice nor .agents/skills/by-choice exists), so there is nothing to adopt; run `labdrian skills install --project-id chosen`
error: skills adopt: refused, so nothing was adopted

# a renamed checkout of the same origin is the same project: adopt asks for its skill, which is not installed there
$ skills adopt --registry <WORLD>/overlay/skills.registry.yaml --source-root <WORLD>/overlay/skills (in renamed-checkout)
exit: 1
--- stdout ---
--- stderr ---
error: skills adopt: skill by-origin is not installed in this project (neither .claude/skills/by-origin nor .agents/skills/by-origin exists), so there is nothing to adopt; run `labdrian skills install --project-id github.com/acme/demo`
error: skills adopt: refused, so nothing was adopted

